[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   step_152: discovery-geometry-conditioned null for the arrival anisotropy (b116).
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   Step 149 (b113) found that the class-1 arrival directions themselves
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   over-concentrate inside the declared 60-deg cap about the resident
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   axis: 48/131 = 36.6% against the 25% uniform-sky fraction (binomial
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   p = 0.0020; the 43/131 = 32.8% figure is the comet-axis cap, kept in
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   b113 T6 for both axes).  That null assumes isotropic arrivals.  A referee's first objection is that cometary
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   perihelion directions are discovery-biased toward the ecliptic band, so
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   a cap sitting near the ecliptic collects excess arrivals by
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   construction.  This step replaces the uniform-sky null with the
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   conditioned nulls that objection requires.
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   Tests
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   T1  ecliptic-latitude-conditioned null.  Each arrival's ecliptic
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   latitude is kept fixed and its longitude is redrawn uniformly
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   (N_DRAW draws over the whole sample).  This is the exact null of
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   "arrivals uniform in longitude given their observed latitude
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   distribution" -- the first-order discovery-pointing model.  The
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   conditioned p is the draw fraction with in-cap fraction >=
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   observed.  Also reports the null median in-cap fraction, which
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   prices how much of the excess the ecliptic band alone explains.
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   T2  Galactic-latitude-conditioned null.  Same construction in the
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   Galactic frame (the axis/cap converted to Galactic coordinates),
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   controlling for concentration toward the Galactic plane rather
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   than the ecliptic.
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   T3  axis-longitude specificity.  The cap is held at the axis's own
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   ecliptic latitude and scanned through longitude: the in-cap
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   fraction is recomputed for every 5-deg longitude placement.
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   The observed placement's rank among the 72 positions tests
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   whether the excess is specific to the axis longitude or generic
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   to the axis's latitude band.
[2026-09-21 15:32:14 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 152]   Subsets: matched (q < 3.1 AU) and all class-1, mirroring step 149.
